  "body": "The situation describes a breakdown in shared mental models regarding household labor. The primary friction point is not the chores themselves, but the ambiguity of verbal agreements combined with dynamic schedules. When plans change and agreements are unwritten, recollections diverge, creating a sense of unreliability. The avoidance behavior indicates that the conflict resolution process itself has become a stressor. To address this, the group should decouple task assignment from personal negotiation by implementing a visible, static system (such as a whiteboard or shared app). Re-engaging the avoiding friend requires a shift in framing: invite them to help design the system rather than to discuss past failures. This lowers the stakes and restores agency.",
